    not_duplicate_of: []  # 8426
    pr_ref:  # 8426
    description: "The drift linter find_axis_drift (in hypergumbo_core.edge_types, used by both the in-tree property test in test_edge_types.py and the pre-commit CLI scripts/check-edge-type-drift) currently scans only packages/*.py for consumer-side *EDGE_TYPE*-named sets. Sets in scripts/ or .agent/ are not checked, so any drift in those locations would slip through.\n\nCONTEXT (for a dev picking this up cold):\n\nADR-0023 (docs/adr/0023-edge-type-relationship-not-endpoints.md) and PR #3459 established the canonical edge-type registry plus the static drift detector. PR #3462 hoisted the detector into find_axis_drift so it is shared between the property test and the pre-commit linter. The detector AST-walks Python files under packages/, looks for module-level assignments whose target name contains EDGE_TYPE, and asserts each set's elements are subsets of the canonical registry.\n\nCurrent scope: packages/*.py excluding tests/ directories. Two locations are NOT scanned:\n\n1. scripts/ — CLI tools and one-off helpers. Some scripts process behavior-map output and may filter by edge_type (e.g., a hypothetical scripts/extract-edges-by-type would have a set or query). Not currently a known offender, but the door is open as the script collection grows.\n\n2. .agent/ — agent-infrastructure hooks (Python scripts under .agent/hooks/_shared/ etc.). Currently no edge-type sets here, but as the agent-state inspection pipeline matures (e.g., a hook that surfaces analyzer output) it could grow some.\n\nThe current narrow scope was deliberate: at PR #3459, the only known consumers were under packages/. Broadening was deferred so the detector could ship and prove out before generalizing.\n\nDELIVERABLES:\n\n1. Broaden find_axis_drift to walk additional roots:\n   - Either: change the function to take a list of search roots instead of a single repo_root (with packages/, scripts/, .agent/ as the default).\n   - Or: keep the single-root signature but walk multiple subtrees internally.\n   The first form is more extensible (future axis-bearing fields in different package layouts can pass their own roots) and aligns with ADR-0024's template intent.\n\n2. Path-exclusion conventions:\n   - Test directories: still excluded (tests/ substring filter, currently in place).\n   - One-off migration helpers: scripts under scripts/migrations/ (if/when such a directory exists) might legitimately reference deprecated edge types. Add an opt-out marker (e.g., a comment annotation, or a path-prefix exclusion) before broadening creates new false positives.\n   - Vendored dependencies: anything under .venv/ or node_modules/ should remain excluded (probably not relevant since walk starts from named roots).\n\n3. Update the calling sites:\n   - test_edge_types.py::test_every_edge_type_named_set_is_a_subset_of_registry calls find_axis_drift(repo_root); needs to either pass the new multi-root parameter or rely on the broader default.\n   - scripts/check-edge-type-drift similarly.\n\n4. Test coverage:\n   - Add unit tests with synthetic fixtures in scripts/ and .agent/ paths to confirm the broader scope catches drift there.\n   - Confirm existing fixture tests in test_edge_types.py still pass.\n\nPOTENTIAL GOTCHAS:\n- .agent/agent_playbooks_protocols_sops_skills/ contains markdown files only, so it will not be scanned anyway (only .py). Hook scripts under .agent/hooks/_shared/ might define edge-type-related sets if any exist now or later — desirable to check.\n- The broader scope might surface NEW drift offenders that the narrower scope was implicitly tolerating. If so, document them in this item's discussion thread (similar to PR #3459's finding of 5 silent bugs in packages/) and resolve case-by-case (registry entry, consumer-side removal, or reclassification) before the broader scope merges as a final fix.\n\nDEPENDENCIES:\n- None HARD. This is a self-contained scope-broadening; can land at any time.\n- SOFT: coordinates with the adjacent loose-end about *EDGE_TYPE* name-filter generalization (separate sibling tracker item) since both touch find_axis_drift. Consider designing jointly to avoid two refactor passes — the cleanest shape supports both per-field name patterns AND multi-root scanning in one parameterization.\n\nACCEPTANCE:\n- find_axis_drift accepts (or implicitly walks) packages/, scripts/, and .agent/ as default search roots.\n- Existing test_edge_types tests pass; new fixtures cover the broader scope.\n- Pre-commit linter (scripts/check-edge-type-drift) still runs cleanly on the live tree.\n- Any new drift offenders surfaced during broadening are documented in this item's discussion thread and resolved (registry entry, consumer-side removal, or reclassification) before the broader scope merges as a final fix.\n\nSIBLINGS:\n- *EDGE_TYPE* name-filter generalization (separate item, file next per the audit-lifecycle session ordering) — currently the substring filter is specific to one field; for Symbol.kind / evidence_type etc. we'd need a different name pattern. Coordinate the design.\n- WI-tavas-voror-rakiv-litog-gatad-zonoz-holah-tugil — 45-value triage. The broadening MIGHT surface emit-site-equivalent drift (consumer sets in scripts/ or .agent/ that reference unregistered values); coordinate so neither rediscovers the other's findings.\n- WI-variv-lujug-fobig-nojit-piraz-lojam-lizil-dosip — drift-linter-tightening. That tightening is gated on Phase 4b; this broadening is independent and can land first.\n\nBACKGROUND: surfaced as loose-end #17 in the audit-lifecycle session (Apr 2026). The narrow scope was deliberate at first ship in PR #3459; broadening was deferred so the detector could prove out before generalizing."  # 8426
    fields: {}  # 8426
